  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing CSS Tokens**\n\nI\'m currently focused on `src/index.css`. Specifically, I\'m thinking about how to declare CSS design tokens correctly within the context of Tailwind CSS v4. I\'m starting to consider how to properly define the font tokens. The initial approach is `@import \"tailwindcss\";` and declaring the root with something like `--font-sans: \'Be Vietnam Pro\', system-ui, -apple...`.\n\n\n**Defining Dark Mode**\n\nI\'ve been working on defining the dark mode tokens. I have the base color definitions in place, and I\'m moving onto the color roles. I\'m currently setting up the mappings. I\'m focusing on consistency in naming and application.\n\n\n**Mapping Utility Classes**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing utility classes for the defined CSS variables. My goal is to streamline the integration of these tokens within Tailwind and component styling. I\'m currently thinking of how to map the token variables directly to utility classes. I\'m considering approaches such as `bg-[var(--bg)]` and helper classes like `.bg-app`, `.text-main`, ensuring an easier transition.\n\n\n"
