  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Project Structure**\n\nI\'m currently focused on structuring the codebase. I\'ve started by outlining the foundational type definitions within `src/types/index.ts`, covering crucial entities like Student, Role, and BehaviorItem. I\'m also preparing to create mock data in `src/data/mockData.ts`, which will include an array of 42 records.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Classroom Layout**\n\nI\'m now visualizing the classroom layout, considering the 6x7 seating arrangement and incorporating elements like teacher\'s table and blackboard. Roles are now clearly defined, including the specific number of students in each group, and overlapping roles, such as the T\341\273\225 tr\306\260\341\273\237ng ki\303\252m B\303\255 th\306\260. I am considering potential name collisions during abbreviation and now I am analyzing the categorization of behaviors.\n\n\n**Refining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now refining the data structures to incorporate specific behavior infractions. These include categories like \"N\341\273\201 n\341\272\277p \342\200\223 V\341\273\207 sinh\" with point deductions, and severe infractions triggering immediate visual warnings. I\'ve expanded the sample records to over 60, spanning three weeks, and included duplicate infraction scenarios for robust testing. I\'m also including the teacher options according to the user\'s initial specifications, such as disabling bonus points and setting a starting point of 100.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_218818115532548782"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Append\":false, \"CodeContent\":\"/**\\n * Type definitions for Qu\341\272\243n l\303\275 N\341\273\201 n\341\272\277p & Thi \304\221ua L\341\273\233p h\341\273\215c 10A5\\n */\\n\\nexport type RoleCode = \'HS\' | \'TT\' | \'LT\' | \'BT\' | \'LP_HT\' | \'LP_LD\' | \'GV\';\\n\\nexport interface StudentRoleBadge {\\n  code: RoleCode;\\n  label: string;\\n  shortLabel: string;\\n  to?: number; // 1, 2, 3, 4 for To truong\\n}\\n\\nexport interface Student {\\n  maHS: string;\\n  hoTen: string;\\n  tenRutGon: string;\\n  to: number; // 1 | 2 | 3 | 4\\n  dayBan: number; // 1 to 6\\n  soBan: number; // 1 to 4\\n  viTriGhe: number; // 1 to 42\\n  vaiTro: RoleCode[];\\n  toTruongTo?: number; // 1..4 if TT\\n  sdtPhuHuynh?: string;\\n  avatarSeed?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport type SeatNodeType = \'ghe\' | \'trong\' | \'loidi\' | \'banGV\' | \'cua\' | \'buc\';\\n\\nexport interface SeatLayoutNode {\\n  hang: number;\\n  cot: number;\\n  loaiO: SeatNodeType;\\n  maHS?: string;\\n  ghiChu?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport type PointType = \'Tru\' | \'Cong\';\\nexport type SeverityLevel = \'Nhe\' | \'Vua\' | \'Nang\';\\n\\nexport interface RuleItem {\\n  maNoiQuy: string;\\n  nhomHanhVi: string; // Chuy\303\252n c\341\272\247n, H\341\273\215c t\341\272\255p, N\341\273\201 n\341\272\277p, Phong tr\303\240o, Lao \304\221\341\273\231ng - V\341\273\207 sinh, \304\220i\341\273\203m c\341\273\231ng\\n  tenHanhVi: string;\\n  loaiDiem: PointType;\\n  diemSo: number; // positive number, applied according to loaiDiem\\n  mucDo: SeverityLevel;\\n  ghim: boolean;\\n  thuTu: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport type RecordStatus = \\n  | \'HieuLuc\' \\n  | \'ChoDuyet\' \\n  | \'DaChapNhan\' \\n  | \'BiTuChoi\' \\n  | \'DaHuy\' \\n  | \'ChoXacNhanTrung\';\\n\\nexport interface DisciplineRecord {\\n  maGhiNhan: string; // UUID\\n  thoiGianMayChu: string; // ISO string\\n  thoiGianMay: string;\\n  ngayHoc: string; // YYYY-MM-DD\\n  buoi: \'Sang\' | \'Chieu\';\\n  tuanHoc: number;\\n  doiTuong: