  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Hierarchical Structure**\n\nI\'m currently breaking down the proposed hierarchical structure for tracking performance metrics. My focus is on the multi-tiered breakdown, from academic year down to individual sessions. This is a very interesting concept, and I\'m keen on establishing the most efficient way to capture the data.\n\n\n**Structuring the Data Hierarchy**\n\nI\'m now deep in the details, working on the data model that will support the hierarchical discipline and emulation tracking structure. I\'m focusing on the `DisciplineRecord` and how to systematically index `namHoc`, `hocKi`, `thang`, `tuanHoc`, `ngayHoc`, and `buoi`. Next, I\'ll be designing the user interface for navigating this hierarchical data with the period selector.\n\n\n**Designing the Navigator Structure**\n\nI\'m now integrating the hierarchical data with the user interface. I\'m focusing on the time period navigator, allowing swift transitions between weekly, monthly, semester, and yearly views. I\'m also planning the student and cadre views. I\'m outlining how to display overall data per time period. For example, student views can compare progress across weeks, months and semesters. I\'m also trying to structure the cadre view to be able to filter through student issues by year, semester, month, week, day, and session. Finally, I\'m making sure that the system can automatically determine the year, semester, month, and week based on the date and time of a session.\n\n\n"
