  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Evaluating Image Quality**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that the generated images are all high-quality. Specifically, I examined the \"Classroom hero banner\" and the \"Cadre leadership crest\" to confirm their visual fidelity. I think they are acceptable for use.\n\n\n**Designing Badge System**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in designing a comprehensive badge system for the cadre. Each role, like \"L\341\273\233p tr\306\260\341\273\237ng\" (Captain), will have a unique title, color, icon, and level. For instance, the Captain will sport a gold badge with a crown or star icon. I\'ve considered how youthful psychology and gamification can be applied to create more appealing titles.\n\n\n**Refining Badge Details**\n\nI\'m currently refining badge details based on feedback. The \"Activity Leader\" will receive an amber-colored badge with a Zap icon, highlighting their role in classroom upkeep. Squad Leaders for each group will have a sapphire-blue badge with a shield or compass, focusing on discipline. Furthermore, I\'ve outlined individual achievements: \"Steel Discipline\" (no violations), \"Spectacular Breakthrough\" (performance improvement), \"Role Model 10A5\" (top 5 discipline), and \"Absolute Punctuality\" (perfect attendance). I am also designing a youth-friendly interface with motivational slogans, animated progress indicators, and streak counters.\n\n\n**Implementing UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI elements. I\'m focusing on incorporating friendly emojis and micro-stickers into the interface. I\'m also developing the `CadreBadge.tsx` component to display duties, permissions, and honors. Further development includes adding golden badges or pins to the seating chart to indicate cadre roles like Captains, Leaders, and Treasurers. I\'m also working on student avatars and student views.\n\n\n"
