    thinking: "**Analyzing Student Data**\n\nI\'ve got the student roster: HS01 (LT), HS02 (BT, TT T\341\273\225 1), HS03 (LP_HT), HS04 (LP_LD), HS12 (TT T\341\273\225 2), HS23 (TT T\341\273\225 3), and HS34 (TT T\341\273\225 4). I\'m starting to think about interface design to be more appealing. The user wants the interface to be visually better. I need to keep the target age group in mind, incorporating images.\n\n\n**Designing Badge Features**\n\nI\'m now diving into feature design. I\'m focusing on a badge system for the class officers (Ban c\303\241n s\341\273\261) and achievement badges for all students (H\341\273\215c sinh). I\'m outlining badge definitions in `/src/data/badgeData.ts`, planning distinct icons, badge styles, and titles for each role, like \"Ch\341\273\211 Huy Tr\306\260\341\273\237ng 10A5\" for the class leader. I\'m also considering unlocked badges based on student performance.\n\n\n**Developing Badge Visuals**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual design of the achievement badges. I\'ve defined specific badges like \"K\341\273\267 Lu\341\272\255t Th\303\251p\" and \"Chi\341\272\277n Th\341\272\247n \304\220\303\272ng Gi\341\273\235,\" considering their meanings and how they\'ll resonate with students. I\'m planning to create components like `CadreBadge.tsx` and `CadreHonorModal.tsx` for a visually appealing and informative display. These components include compact badges for quick views and full emblem cards, and even achievement badge lists.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Interface**\n\nI\'m now integrating visuals to enhance the user interface. I\'m focusing on appealing to the 15-16 age group with visual personality and color, steering clear of anything garish. I\'m incorporating a hero banner, a motivational slogan ticker, and student profile cards featuring a gold trophy for high scores and a leadership crest for cadres. I\'m also planning to enhance the SeatGrid with small insignia on student desks to visually distinguish class officers. I\'m adding initial avatar badges with gradients, too.\n\n\n"
