  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering UI Enhancements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the implications of enabling drag-and-drop functionality within `SeatGrid.tsx`. The goal is to allow users, specifically GVCN (likely a teacher), to intuitively re-arrange student seating, and potentially reposition classroom elements like doors and desks. I\'m exploring how this impacts the existing component structure and if UI modifications are needed for this to function well.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Features**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the interactive aspects. I\'m focusing on the \"Tr\303\254nh S\341\272\257p X\341\272\277p S\306\241 \304\220\341\273\223 L\341\273\233p H\341\273\215c\" design, particularly the Drag & Drop and Touch & Click-to-Swap modes. The goal is to provide intuitive UX for GVCN, utilizing HTML5 drag and drop, while ensuring mobile compatibility with a click-to-swap method, with appropriate visual feedback. I\'m exploring how student and classroom element data will be updated.\n\n\n**Developing Structural Flexibility**\n\nI\'m now focused on enabling GVCN to not just rearrange student seats, but also the classroom\'s architectural elements. I\'m visualizing a tool selector palette, with elements like teacher desks and doors, allowing click-to-change functionality for cell types, and presets for quickly setting up classroom arrangements. I\'m also considering the user experience of switching seat layouts within the application.\n\n\n**Implementing Visual Rewards**\n\nI\'m now integrating visual cues to enhance the interface. I plan to use emojis to identify student cadres on the seating chart, and I\'m designing a `CadreBadge.tsx` alongside a `CadreHonorsModal.tsx` to display full leadership crests. In `StudentView.tsx`, I\'ll display honor trophies and achievement badges for good performance. I\'m also adding a hero banner illustration and dynamic student avatars with colorful initials.\n\n\n"
