  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Classroom Layout**\n\nOkay, so I\'m focusing on the initial row in `ClassroomLayoutEditor.tsx`. Specifically, when the seating arrangement mode is active (`mode === \'seating\'`) and the row index is zero. I\'m visualizing a clean text strip for the top row, representing the teacher\'s area. I\'ve got the left text as \"B\303\240n GV\", center as \"\342\200\224 B\341\272\242NG \342\200\224\", and right as \"C\341\273\255a ch\303\255nh\".\n\n\n**Refining Row Rendering**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the rendering of row zero in both seating and structure modes. The quick buttons in structure mode, allowing easy swapping of \"Teacher Desk\" and \"Front Door\", feel intuitive. I\'m focusing on \"clean text\" rendering for row zero, specifically updating `MOCK_SEAT_LAYOUT` in `mockData.ts` and adjusting `SeatGrid.tsx` for a \"unboxed text header,\" making this top row display a text-only representation.\n\n\n**Optimizing Visual Display**\n\nI\'m now implementing clean text indicators for specific rows, improving the UI. Row zero, which is the teacher\'s area, and row eight, indicating the back of the classroom, will have text-only representations. This avoids clunky empty boxes when the back row is student-free. I\'ve focused on using text for the top and bottom rows to maintain a clean presentation.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
