  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing SeatGrid Logic**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `SeatGrid.tsx` component. I\'m specifically examining the logic for row index 0. The goal is to determine if \"B\303\240n GV\" (Teacher\'s Desk) is positioned to the left or right of the nodes in that initial row.\n\n\n**Determining \"Ban GV\" Placement**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing how \"B\303\240n GV\" (Teacher\'s Desk) is positioned relative to other elements, specifically \"C\341\273\255a ch\303\255nh\" (Main Door), within the initial row. I\'ve narrowed it down to using the `isBanGVLeft` variable\'s logic. This logic determines if the desk is positioned to the left or right, based on column indices. Now, the `isBanGVLeft` variable\'s logic seems to be sound for this positioning.\n\n\n**Interpreting Component Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the component\'s structure to understand the layout logic, specifically focusing on the conditional rendering within the JSX. I\'m examining how the \"C\341\273\255a ch\303\255nh\" (Main Door), \"B\341\272\243ng\" (Board), and \"B\303\240n GV\" (Teacher\'s Desk) are arranged when `rowIndex` is 0. I\'m trying to determine their order. Also, I am looking at how the \"C\341\273\255a sau\" (Back Door) is rendered when `rowIndex` is 8.\n\n\n"
