    thinking: "**Examining Seat Layout**\n\nI\'ve been looking closely at the `mockData.ts` file, and specifically the `MOCK_SEAT_LAYOUT`. I\'ve noted that cot 0, 1 correspond to `banGV`, cot 3, 4 represent `buc`, and cot 6, 7 stand for `cua`. I\'m now turning my attention to the `App.tsx` file, focusing on the state initialization for the `layout` variable.\n\n\n**Refining Layout Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing a migration check within `App.tsx` to handle potential discrepancies in saved layouts. If a legacy layout is detected, specifically one where the first seat is \'cua\', I\'ll update it to the new configuration with \'banGV\' and re-save. Concurrently, I\'m examining `ClassroomLayoutEditor.tsx`, specifically lines 496-510, to refine the rendering of the first row in seating mode. The aim is to present a cleaner, unboxed text row instead of the 8-grid boxes.\n\n\n**Analyzing Seat Display**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on `SeatGrid.tsx` and how it renders the first row. The logic to display \'banGV\' (teacher\'s desk) and \'cua\' (door) is now clear. I\'m assessing the `isBanGVLeft` variable; the rendering dynamically updates the layout display based on the teacher\'s desk\'s position relative to the door\'s, determining which side the teacher\'s desk appears on. I\'m evaluating its visual impact and considering potential edge cases.\n\n\n**Evaluating Seat Row Rendering**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of how the first and last rows are rendered, particularly within `SeatGrid.tsx`. I\'ve looked at the display of the teacher\'s desk and the door, and I\'m evaluating the presentation of \"cua\", \"bang\", and \"banGV\" within those rows. I am checking the function `applyPresetTeacherDesk`, and its role in dynamically applying the teacher desk\'s position. I\'m focusing on the visual cues and text labels.\n\n\n**Implementing Seat Assignments**\n\nI\'m now integrating logic to dynamically assign seat types (\'banGV\', \'cua\', \'buc\') based on the \'side\' parameter, which indicates the teacher\'s desk\'s position. I\'m focusing on the mapping function and how it assigns these seats when the `hang` is 0. I will ensure that the seat types and notes are correctly updated within the layout, depending on if the teacher\'s desk is on the left or the right.\n\n\n"
