  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Classroom Layouts**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `applyPresetTeacherDesk` function within the `ClassroomLayoutEditor.tsx` file. Specifically, I\'m examining how it handles moving the teacher\'s desk to either the left or right side, effectively swapping its position with the \"C\341\273\255a ch\303\255nh\". This involves mapping the existing layout to generate a new configuration.\n\n\n**Refining Seat Node Logic**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down into the logic within the function, specifically the conditional block that determines seat types (\'banGV\', \'cua\', \'buc\') based on the \'side\' parameter (\'left\' or \'right\'). I\'m focusing on how the column (cot) values are used to assign these types, essentially mapping the layout by changing the values. I\'m looking at how the function swaps the positions of the teacher\'s desk and the main door.\n\n\n**Evaluating Desk-Door Swap**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the `handleToggleDeskDoorSwap` function. My focus is on how it detects the teacher\'s desk position and triggers the `applyPresetTeacherDesk` function. I\'m noting how the conditional logic determines whether to swap the desk to the left or right, depending on its initial column value. I\'m also examining how the function updates the UI with feedback about the desk and door\'s new positions.\n\n\n**Observing Conditional Rendering**\n\nI\'m now examining the conditional rendering within the layout representation. Specifically, I\'m noting how the `isBanGVLeft` variable affects the display of the teacher\'s desk and main door. The goal is to determine how the component dynamically swaps these elements in the UI based on this boolean. I\'m focusing on the component\'s structure and its logic that shows \"B\303\240n GV\" on the left when `isBanGVLeft` is true.\n\n\n**Interpreting UI Element Display**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on how the UI component renders the \"C\341\273\255a ch\303\255nh\" (main door) and \"B\303\240n GV\" (teacher\'s desk) elements, specifically examining the conditional rendering logic within the component. I\'m noting how the component uses the `isBanGVLeft` variable to determine whether to display the teacher\'s desk and main door together, and how it renders differently based on the mode.\n\n\n**Examining Structural Display**\n\nI\'m now examining how the component displays \"C\341\273\255a sau\" and \"Cu\341\273\221i l\341\273\233p\" in the \"structure\" mode, which are rendered as unboxed text labels in the \"seating\" mode. I\'m focusing on the component\'s structure and the logic responsible for dynamically swapping the desk and the main door on the UI in different modes. The rendering of these elements seems to depend on the \"mode\" variable and the `handleToggleDeskDoorSwap` function.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
