  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering New Application Features**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the user\'s request. My aim is to incorporate a \"Games\" section into the teacher\'s interface. Specifically, I\'m thinking of including around ten popular, engaging games suitable for calling students to the board. The goal aligns with ultra-mode and my front-end design goals: a universal design constitution, appealing to gaming sensibilities, while avoiding common AI pitfalls, making it distinctive, fun, and high-quality.\n\n\n**Analyzing Student Preferences**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing student appeal and computer usage verification within the \"Games\" section. Specifically, I\'m delving into the user\'s request, focusing on \"\341\273\250ng d\341\273\245ng\" or a \"Ti\341\273\207n \303\255ch & Tr\303\262 ch\306\241i\" addition to the teacher\'s interface. My research narrows to 10 popular classroom games, starting with a Lucky Spin Wheel, incorporating the specific 42 students of class 10A5 for a targeted, engaging experience. I\'m aiming for interactive mini-games for board participation.\n\n\n**Developing Game Interaction Methods**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the interaction methods within the \"Games\" section. I\'m exploring options to filter by student groups like T\341\273\225 1, 2, 3, or 4, or select from all 42 students. Specifically, I\'m considering features like \"Mystery Lucky Boxes\" with glowing cards that reveal student avatars and fun missions, and a \"Lucky Slot Machine\" with animated reels displaying student names. I\'m also planning \"Lucky Red Envelopes\" for a chance drawing, and interactive race minigames to keep things engaging.\n\n\n**Designing Race & Selection Games**\n\nI\'m now implementing the new ideas. I\'ve designed a race minigame with 4-6 student racers or teams with speed boosts and a finish line. I\'ve also incorporated the Hot Potato/Ticking Bomb game with a fast-cycling screen and explosive reveal. The Space Mission game with a rocket launch and student commander landing is nearly complete. I\'m also thinking about a Claw Machine with plushies and student balls for selection.\n\n\n"
