  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding New Functionality**\n\nI\'m currently focused on incorporating a new \"\341\273\251ng d\341\273\245ng\" section for teachers, as requested. The idea is to populate it with about ten popular classroom games, which would be a neat add-on. I\'m exploring how to best integrate it into the existing navigation, considering the current tabs: overview, record, explanations, roster, rules, import_export, and settings. My goal is a user-friendly and intuitive placement.\n\n\n**Designing New Game Features**\n\nI\'m now diving into the design of the \"\341\273\250ng d\341\273\245ng\" tab, focusing on the visual appeal and functionality of the classroom games. I\'ve decided to go with a \"Kho \341\273\251ng d\341\273\245ng \360\237\216\262\" label, aiming for an engaging gamepad or sparkles icon. I\'m also planning to add a quick launcher button to the overview banner for \"Tr\303\262 ch\306\241i g\341\273\215i b\341\272\243ng \360\237\216\262\" to ensure ease of access. I\'m currently exploring the `lucide-react` library for the perfect icons and will design ten classroom games, starting with the interactive \"V\303\262ng Quay May M\341\272\257n.\"\n\n\n**Developing New Game Mechanics**\n\nI\'m now detailing some new game ideas. For the random name picker, I\'m thinking of adding visual effects like deceleration, click ticks, flapper bounce, and confetti explosion on the stop. It will show the chosen student\'s avatar, seat number, and options to re-roll, note infractions or give points, or exclude them from the next round. I\'m also planning a ticking bomb and a slot machine, each with interactive elements and sound effects.\n\n\n**Designing New Interactions**\n\nI\'m now detailing some new game ideas. I\'m imagining a \"R\303\272t Th\341\272\273 Nh\303\242n Ph\341\272\251m\" game with shimmering cards that flip with 3D rotation and golden sparkles, revealing funny RPG titles. There\'s also a \"\304\220ua Xe F1\" race with turbo effects and a checkered flag reveal, and a \"B\341\272\257n T\303\252n L\341\273\255a V\305\251 Tr\341\273\245\" with a countdown, galaxy visuals, and a beam-down reveal. I\'m exploring lever animations with mechanical tumbler sound effects.\n\n\n**Expanding Game Concepts**\n\nI\'m now detailing some new game ideas. I\'m visualizing a \"B\341\273\221c Th\304\203m L\303\254 X\303\254\" game with swaying envelopes that tear open with golden confetti and reveal a student\'s name and fortune. Also, I\'m working on a \"M\303\241y G\341\272\257p Th\303\272\" game with a classic claw machine, with plushie capsules that open to reveal the student, and a \"Ma Tr\341\272\255n \303\224 S\341\273\221\" with a laser sweep reveal. Finally, I\'m designing a DJ drop for class transitions.\n\n\n**Adding New Interactions**\n\nI\'ve been envisioning a DJ drop game, with a neon turntable and a groovy equalizer. When the teacher clicks \"Drop the Needle,\" there\'s a scratch sound, a spotlight on the selected student, applause, and disco lights. Moreover, I\'m integrating a Web Audio API synthesizer for all the sound effects, like clicks and explosions. There\'s also a mute/unmute toggle. I\'m also planning to filter by team, gender, and student history. A quick action button will then allow for bonus points or deductions.\n\n\n"
