  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing UI Element**\n\nI\'ve been examining the avatar UI element within `StudentView.tsx`, specifically lines 247-254. Focusing on the styling, I\'m noting the use of a gradient background (`bg-gradient-to-tr`), rounded corners, and absolute positioning. Also considering how this styling could be improved or generalized.\n\n\n**Refining Avatar Interaction**\n\nI\'m now integrating an avatar upload feature. I\'m thinking of passing `onUpdateStudentAvatar` down from `App.tsx`. I\'ve added a camera/upload icon directly on the avatar, opening an `AvatarUploadModal`. The modal will support drag-and-drop or click-to-choose, with an instant client-side preview and crop. Also, I think some preset avatars (emojis/illustrations) would be great for a quicker selection.\n\n\n**Expanding Avatar Usage**\n\nI\'m now expanding the avatar\'s application throughout the student\'s representation. I\'m focusing on lines 48-52 in `SeatGrid.tsx` and the relevant sections of game components. I\'m ensuring that the student\'s avatar is displayed consistently: in the seat desks and within all the calling games (Wheel, Cards, etc.) and in Cadre honors and rankings. I\'ve confirmed that the `object-cover` property works as desired. This provides a more personalized experience.\n\n\n**Designing Game Mechanics**\n\nI\'m now outlining some new game mechanics, thinking about the student experience. The \"Wheel of Fortune\" with student names is the classic first idea, complete with spin mechanics and victory animation. Then there\'s the \"Hot Seat\" with a ticking bomb, and an explosion effect. I also thought about a \"Lucky Slot Machine\", with different reels showing classes, names, and challenges. Next, \"Mystery Cards\", or \"Gacha\" game, reveal student names with a fun, glowing animation. Finally, I\'m envisioning a \"Turbo Race\", a fun F1 race.\n\n\n**Developing Game Selection**\n\nI\'m now iterating on game selection mechanics for student engagement. I\'m focusing on new game designs. I\'m imagining a \"Turbo Race\" down a racetrack with smoke trails and nitro boosts. The winning car crosses the checkered flag to reveal the selected student! \"Cosmic Rocket Launch\" is also a thought, with a countdown to lift-off and beam down the student\'s name from space.\nI\'m picturing \"Golden Ticket & Lucky Red Envelopes\", which display good luck messages!\n\n\n**Conceptualizing Game Interface**\n\nI\'m now integrating DJ-themed mechanics: a glowing turntable with equalizer waves. The user \"drops the needle\" for a scratch sound, spotlight, and applause. The feature set includes group and gender filters, an \"exclude called\" option with a counter and reset, and a sound toggle using Web Audio API. The winning modal will display the student\'s photo, name, group, and seat, along with actions to record points, violations, re-spin, or close. I am working on the file structure.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Structures**\n\nI\'m structuring the data models, specifically adding `avatarUrl?: string;` to `Student`. I\'m also considering dedicated types for game data, for a smoother flow. I\'ve begun working with Web Audio API for a series of fun sound effects, too.\n\n\n\n"
