  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Hierarchy**\n\nI\'m focusing intently on the precise user request for the time hierarchy: school year > semester > week > session. I recognize the 19-week/semester structure for semesters 1 and 2, which is absolutely clear in the instructions provided. The structure can be neatly implemented.\n\n\n**Defining the Time Structure**\n\nI\'ve clarified the four-level hierarchy as N\304\203m h\341\273\215c > H\341\273\215c k\303\254 > Tu\341\272\247n > Bu\341\273\225i. H\341\273\215c k\303\254 1 spans weeks 1-19, and H\341\273\215c k\303\254 2 spans weeks 20-38. Bu\341\273\225i options are S\303\241ng, Chi\341\273\201u, or T\341\272\245t c\341\272\243. Filtering is now straightforward, with dependent selections. I\'m focusing on `getTimeHierarchyFromDate` logic to assign Hoc Ki based on the week number and updating the display format to align with the hierarchy.\n\n\n\n"
