  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Student Data**\n\nI\'ve directly assigned genders (\'Nam\' or \'Nu\') to each student in `MOCK_STUDENTS`: HS01 is Nam, HS02 is Nu, HS03-HS05 are all Nam. I\'m moving methodically to ensure each data point is accurate.\n\n\n**Expanding Student Data**\n\nI\'ve continued assigning genders. Now, I have assigned genders (\'Nam\' or \'Nu\') to a larger set of students, from HS07 to HS37, ensuring accuracy in the data. I\'m focusing on consistency.\n\n\n**Assigning Final Genders**\n\nI\'ve finished assigning genders to the remaining students, from HS38 to HS42, and have ensured consistency. I\'m building out a helper function to determine if a student is female, including using regular expressions on their names, for better accuracy.\n\nI\'m now integrating this information into the seat grid, visually differentiating between genders with color-coded backgrounds and borders for seats, and a legend. This visual cue should allow anyone viewing the chart to instantly understand which seats are assigned to which gender. Finally, I\'m thinking about the requirement around seats near the back door.\n\n\n**Refining Seat Grid**\n\nI\'ve updated the visual representation of the seat grid to meet the requirement about the back row. I\'ve modified the back-row label in `SeatGrid.tsx` to center \"\342\200\224 CU\341\273\220I L\341\273\232P \342\200\224\" with improved styling for a clearer presentation of the row\'s significance. I focused on making the information more prominent.\n\n\n**Simplifying Interface Design**\n\nI\'ve simplified the classroom layout editor. I\'ve centered \"\342\200\224 CU\341\273\220I L\341\273\232P \342\200\224\" in `ClassroomLayoutEditor.tsx`. I\'ve removed the structure editing features as requested, streamlining the interface to focus solely on student seating arrangement, with a clear header and helpful tips for teachers. Students are now color-coded by gender.\n\n\n**Implementing New Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating new features into the application. First, I\'ll add a new \"Apps\" tab to the teacher dashboard with a calling games hub, with the appropriate visual cues. Then, I\'ll allow students to upload avatars by adding a camera button to the student view. Finally, I\'ll incorporate a data import card for time-related data. I will start by updating the student type definition to include gender.\n\n\n"
