    thinking: "**Revising Imports Now**\n\nI\'m currently updating the imports in `StudentView.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m refactoring the import statement at the top. This involves including React\'s hooks (`useState`, `useMemo`), along with essential components such as `User`, `LayoutGrid`, `Trophy`, and several others from the UI library, `AlertCircle`, `CheckCircle2`, `Clock`, `MessageSquare`, `X`, `Send`, `Sparkles`. I\'m making sure all dependencies are accounted for.\n\n\n**Expanding Imports Further**\n\nI\'ve significantly expanded the imports in `StudentView.tsx`. Now I\'ve added icons from `lucide-react`: `Award`, `Flame`, `Shield`, `Star`, `BookOpen`, `Calendar`, `ChevronRight`, `Camera`, `ChevronLeft`. Also, I\'ve incorporated several type definitions and utilities needed for managing student data and summaries, including imports for types such as `Student`, `SeatLayoutNode`, `DisciplineRecord`, `StudentWeekSummary`, `TeacherSettings`, and `HierarchyPeriodFilter`. I\'ve also integrated new components for the seat grid, cadre badges, modal, and filter.\n\n\n**Analyzing Component Props**\n\nI\'m now focused on refining the props used by the `StudentView` component. I\'m looking at how I\'m handling data like `DisciplineRecord`, `StudentWeekSummary`, and the `TeacherSettings`. Additionally, I\'m examining the `onSubmitExplanation` and `onUpdateStudentAvatar` callback functions. I\'m also planning on integrating the state related to the avatar modal. The calculated `myRank` and `myFrame` values are being scrutinized and optimized for reusability with `useMemo`, and I am removing the slogan banner in favor of a clean badge.\n\n\n**Refining Display Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the UI display logic within `StudentView.tsx`. I\'ve added a section that displays school year info, utilizing `CURRENT_SCHOOL_YEAR`. I\'m integrating a \"Cadre Quick Button\" that shows up when `isCadre` is true, enabling the user to open a modal. I\'m removing the cheesy slogan banner. I\'m also adding a conditional render which will show my score if the active tab is not equal to `my_score`.\n\n\n**Adjusting Button Actions**\n\nI\'m currently revising the button action flow in the student view. I\'ve added a button to navigate back to \"My Page\" with a chevron icon and text indicating the active tab context. The button\'s style and functionality are being refined for smoother user interaction, and I\'m ensuring the component handles conditional rendering based on the active tab state. I\'m also ensuring the avatar and camera button are aligned correctly, and using the correct frame.\n\n\n**Determining Student Role**\n\nI\'m working on logic to determine a student\'s role and display the appropriate badge. I\'ve implemented a conditional chain to check the `vaiTro` property. Currently, it covers \'BT\', \'LP_HT\', \'LP_LD\', and \'TT\' roles, dynamically setting the badge based on these values. If no role is found, the badge is undefined. I am also determining how to conditionally render the student avatar with a fallback.\n\n\n**Implementing Avatar Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now integrating avatar enhancements. I\'ve added an avatar frame component with conditional styling, using a dynamic background based on student name abbreviation. I\'ve implemented a seat badge with student position and a camera upload button that opens the avatar modal. The camera button is positioned correctly and styled appropriately, and the seat badge is also correctly implemented and styled. I\'m ensuring everything is positioned correctly within the layout.\n\n\n\n"
