    thinking: "**Updating the UI**\n\nI\'ve been working on UI updates. Specifically, in `TeacherDashboard.tsx`, I just changed line 340. The original text describing students, desks, and school values has been replaced with more specific academic year data: \"N\304\203m h\341\273\215c 2026-2027\".\n\n\n**Adding a Feature Card**\n\nI\'m now integrating a new feature card right under the existing banner. It will showcase \"Calling Games\". The card\'s content includes a title in Vietnamese (\"10 Tr\303\262 Ch\306\241i G\341\273\215i H\341\273\215c Sinh L\303\252n B\341\272\243ng\"), a \"NEW & HOT\" badge, and a placeholder for more detail. I\'m aiming for an appealing design with a gradient background, shadow, and icon to capture attention.\n\n\n**Listing Game Ideas**\n\nI\'ve been brainstorming game concepts. The current list includes \"V\303\262ng quay may m\341\272\257n,\" \"Bom n\341\273\225 ch\341\272\255m,\" \"M\303\241y g\341\272\257p th\303\272,\" \"\304\220ua xe F1,\" \"Slot machine,\" \"B\303\240i tarot,\" \"T\303\252n l\341\273\255a,\" \"Bao l\303\254 x\303\254,\" \"Ma tr\341\272\255n 42 \303\264,\" and \"DJ \304\221\304\251a than.\" These ideas are geared toward interactive elements for the feature card, and are great for student engagement.\n\n\n"
